alias ExitStatus = std::process::ExitStatus;
alias Inputs = std::process::Inputs;

public fn run(inputs: Inputs) -> status: ExitStatus pure waits doc "The layout_oracle entry, invoked as `layout_oracle MODE REPS PAGE UA [SUFFIX=SHEET ...]` with the style oracle's arguments, from the repository root, with the installed fonts copied into build/fonts. It loads the page and its sheets with pkg::oracle::page, computes styles and loads the fonts, then: dump matches the fonts, builds and lays out the page once and writes the format of tests/layout/layout_oracle.mjs to standard output; boxes, text and layout repeat REPS times the stage's parts in nested order, so that the time of each part is the difference between consecutive modes: boxes builds the box tree, text also matches each font group's faces (pkg::layout::text::pick_fonts) and prepares every paragraph's text (font matching, shaping and break opportunities), and layout also lays the tree out; each prints the mode, the element, context and paragraph counts and REPS. nodes (REPS 0) lists the nodes of the document in tree order, without styles or fonts: an element as `E NODE DEPTH NAME DESCENDANTS INDEX` (NODE the node identifier, DEPTH the number of element ancestors, DESCENDANTS the number of elements below it, INDEX its position in the traversal), a Text node as `T NODE PARENT LENGTH DATA` (LENGTH in bytes, DATA with backslash written `\\` and line feed `\n`), and last `N COUNT`, the number of nodes the document holds. edit takes the path of an edit script in place of REPS: it loads the page, applies the script's S lines, runs the whole pipeline (traversal, styles, font matching, layout, placement) on the live document and prints `base hash H bytes N`, H being the FNV-1a 64-bit hash of the dump in 16 hexadecimal digits and N its size; then, for each edit line in order, it applies the edit to the live document, reruns the pipeline and prints `edit I hash H bytes N` (I from 1); after a T or D edit, which it also applies to a layout kept across edits with pkg::layout's text_changed and update, the line ends in ` inc same` or ` inc DIFF` as the kept layout's dump is or is not byte for byte the rebuilt one's, or ` inc refused` when text_changed or update refused the edit (a P line's dump of a differing edit is followed by the line `inc dump` and the incremental dump), and the kept layout becomes the rebuilt one after a difference, a refusal or any other edit. incremental takes the script as edit does, applies each T or D edit only to the kept layout and prints `edit I us U prepared R contexts C paragraphs P held_entries H entries E`, U the microseconds text_changed and update took on the clock and the rest pkg::layout's update_counts, or `edit I inc refused` after rebuilding the layout, and rebuilds it after any other edit, printing `edit I full`. The script has one operation per line: `S CSS` adds the rest of the line as an author style sheet after the page's own, only before the first edit; `T NODE OFFSET TEXT` inserts the rest of the line (with `\\` and `\n` resolved) into a Text node's data at a byte offset; `D NODE OFFSET LENGTH` deletes bytes of a Text node's data; `C ELEMENT TOKEN` and `K ELEMENT TOKEN` add a token to and remove a token from an element's class attribute; `B PARENT BEFORE TEXT` inserts a new HTML p element holding one Text node of the text into PARENT before the node BEFORE (`-` for the end) and prints `created NODE` before the edit's line; `X NODE` detaches a node; `P I` requests the full dump of edit I (0 for the unedited document) after its hash line. The style attributes and presentational hints are recorded once, at load, by element position, so an edit that adds or removes an element leaves them attached to the old positions. Exits 2 when the invocation, a file, the page, the style stage, the layout stage or an edit script line fails.";
